Real world application 3: 💾 Binary File for Fixed-Size Records

📌 Brief Description

The Binary File for Fixed-Size Records program demonstrates how fixed-size metadata records can be stored efficiently in a binary file.

The example stores image metadata such as width, height, and image format, writes the records using binary file operations, and then reads them sequentially.

🔑 Key Concepts

- 💾 Binary file handling
- ⚙️ "ios::binary"
- ✍️ "write()" operation
- 📖 "read()" operation
- 📦 Fixed-size structures
- 🔄 Sequential record retrieval

🌍 Real-World Application

This technique can be used in multimedia applications, image-processing systems, embedded systems, and applications requiring compact record storage.

🎯 Main Purpose

To demonstrate efficient storage and retrieval of fixed-size records using binary files.
